@startuml activity_protect
' Protecting an image (thesis ch. 4.3)
start
:Seller uploads original (PNG/JPEG/HEIC);
:Normalise: EXIF rotation, RGB, longer side <= 1600 px;
:Pre-check: run the detection pipeline on the upload;
if (Carries one of our IDs, matches a registered\noriginal, or a valid foreign TraceMark ID?) then (yes)
  :Refuse (HTTP 409) with the reason;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Store original, create product;
:Reserve copy ID (20 bits);
:Payload = ID + HMAC tag (10 bits), XOR mask,\nBCH(63,30,t=6) -> 63 bits;
:Encoder (v3/v4, with secret key for v4)\nresidual at 128 px, NVF mask, upsampled;
if (DCT layer enabled?) then (yes)
  :Keep reference; add keyed DCT spread spectrum\n(luminance, HMAC(key, copy ID));
endif
:Measure PSNR / SSIM, write diff image;
:Append signed, hash-chained registration record\n(SHA-256 of original and copy, UTC time, optional RFC 3161);
:Register original's SIFT fingerprint and copy IDs;
:Return protected copy for publishing;
stop
@enduml
